    "by": "claude",
    "date": "2026-11-17",
    "note": "Security update from 2.9.0. The wheel's 162 dns/ modules are identical to the v2.9.2 tag on github.com/rthalley/dnspython; attestation verifies, same publisher as the reviewed 2.9.0 (rthalley/dnspython publish.yml, env pypi); OSV: no advisory for 2.9.2. The diff from 2.9.0 (58 files) is 2.9.1's documented hardening (random query ids, xfr response checks, RRSIG/REVOKE checks, strict base64/NSEC3/TLSA/SSHFP/LOC parsing, quic server name, entropy pool sha256) plus 2.9.2's WKS bound (bitmap <= 8192 bytes, service 0-65535); new imports only datetime, sys (version check), dns.entropy, dns.dnssectypes, cryptography's InvalidSignature. YARA capability hits are the same strings as 2.9.0's (resolv.conf read, /dev/urandom, a docstring 'system ('). No .pth, no hook, no binary. Upstream's doc/whatsnew.rst in the tag carries a stray merge-conflict marker (docs only, not in the wheel)."
